Vitamix 6300
I’d been waiting for a while to make a decision. When I saw that the Meiya 6300 was on sale, and the price was the same as it was for overseas purchases from Central Asia, I quickly bought it.
I placed the order on September 2nd, and the expected delivery date was September 21st. However, it arrived on September 12th, which is almost 10 days earlier than expected! The speed is really impressive!
The packaging box isn’t very large; we used the original Vitamix packaging directly. Amazon doesn’t seem to worry about the package getting damaged during the long shipping journey across the ocean either!
The machine looks quite new and comes with all the necessary accessories. However, the cup shakes excessively when placed on the stand; I’m actually afraid that it might fly out when I turn on the machine!
Asked a friend who had 5200 followers on Weibo, and he described it as not being this loose to me.
The recipes that come randomly with the product are all in English, and it’s quite frustrating to read them. I couldn’t find any Chinese versions of them online either, which is really a problem!
As soon as I received the goods, I quickly bought a transformer. It should take about 3 days to arrive, and then I’ll really get to work on setting it up properly!
It’s never been opened (or disassembled).
The battery is in use.
I really want to dissect it and see what's inside its belly.
Later on, I thought about the possibility that if I opened it and was disappointed, it would be a waste of all that money. And if I opened it and was satisfied, then reassembling it would be difficult, and using it would be unpleasant.
Never mind; let’s just assume that Sony uses high-quality battery cells anyway.
As for the detailed explanation of battery power consumption, it would probably make most people feel uneasy upon reading it.
I’m fine; I used to work for a mobile phone factory for a long time. Apart from not understanding how electrical circuits work, I kind of consider myself a “half-battery engineer” – I can handle the situation.
Operating system is generally not great.
It took some time to get used to it, and overall the picture quality is okay; I can’t really tell any difference. However, the system itself is quite complicated to use. The startup time is noticeably slow, and it’s difficult to make proper settings. As for the additional software that comes with it, there’s no need even to comment on it—the response speed is just average at best. Compared to the system at my colleague’s home, there’s a huge difference in performance.
I read the comments saying that the design is very user-friendly, but I don’t see anything particularly user-friendly about it. The placement of the buttons on the remote control—which are frequently used for moving up, down, left, right, and navigating back—is really not commendable.
So, just think of it as a TV, plus some additional components like a TV box or the like.
At present, there is no official Amazon feedback channel to be found; therefore, one can only leave feedback in the product reviews section.
1. On March 29th, I purchased this book for 31 yuan through the pre-order option. It was indicated that the book would be delivered to my device on March 31st. At that time, it was still not possible to preview the book on the official Amazon website (because it had not been released yet).
The book that was pushed to devices on March 31 had blank content and only a message saying “Please wait.” Meanwhile, the price of the electronic version of this book on Amazon has dropped to 18 yuan.
3. Over the past couple of days, I’ve repeatedly tried to delete the empty books that were downloaded to the device and then synced it again, but I was unable to obtain the electronic version of “The Nature of Business” which contains the actual content. However, I’ve seen that the book is now available for preview on the Amazon official website.
I have a few thoughts at the moment.
1. The issue of price is actually not the most important one. What really matters right now is how to convert the empty books on the Kindle into books with actual content, rather than always having to wait for the downloads to complete with the message “Please wait…”
2. The books that are pre-purchased should probably not be bought again in the future. After all, if there is a delay in the release of the book and you try to download another copy with empty (meaning no content) files, the process seems to be very complicated.
3. I hope Amazon provides a normal channel to report such issues; when there is any doubt about downloading or using e-books, one can have an outlet to feedback (e.g., through tickets or online customer service). This can be similar to how Microsoft’s official store handles it.
The lonely little lion
When I got the book, I thought it would be as simple as The Lost Piece of Paper, but turns out there's still a lot of text!
I read it three times in total before finishing reading the book to the children. It’s about a little lion that can shoot guns, and a little lion who loves to eat juice-flavored lollipops.
The scene of the lion eating the hunter is a bit uncomfortable, and the arrangement of being eaten by animals is a bit unacceptable to modern urban people.
In the end, this little lion that had succeeded in human society lost itself. It was no longer entirely a lion, nor entirely a human being.
Finally, only the back of the little lion is visible; it’s unknown where he has gone.
Maybe many years from now, the image of this little lion will still be remembered by the grown-up children. One day, it might be brought to mind casually, and perhaps it will touch or inspire her in some way.
